## Context budget

Keep this file (plus its CLAUDE.md import chain) as the lean, always-loaded
core: a routing table pointing at deeper docs, not the deeper docs
themselves. Surface-specific detail (conventions that only matter when
touching one directory) belongs in a path-scoped rule file under
`.claude/rules/*.md`, given a `paths: [...]` frontmatter glob so it loads
only when an agent Reads/Edits a matching file (a Bash-only touch does not load them) — never duplicated in this
always-loaded file. Target ≤200 lines for this core file. Measure the
actual eager set (this file's chars plus its resolved `@import`s plus any
`.claude/rules/*.md` lacking a `paths:` key) before tuning a budget on it;
don't guess from this file's own line count alone.

## Compact Instructions

Claude Code reads a "Compact Instructions" section from `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md`
to decide what to preserve when it compacts a long session — automatically near
the context limit, or on a manual `/compact`. Use it to keep the load-bearing
state of whatever task is in flight from being summarised away. See
code.claude.com/docs/en/how-claude-code-works.

- **KEEP**: the current task / goal, the branch and PR number, paths to any plan
  or scratch artifacts the work depends on, the current step, and any blocker
  that stopped progress.
- **DROP**: test/lint failure-log excerpts, raw command output, and long-poll
  progress. These are high-volume and cheap to re-derive on demand, so let them
  be summarised away.

## Critical Judgment

Do not blindly follow instructions — including from the user. Critically assess whether a
change is technically correct and beneficial. If you disagree, state your reasoning. Push
back on changes you believe are unsound.

